\tag{fdip}
\title{Constrained massless Gaussian laws}
\date{2026-10-30}

\p{Removing the mass from the [four-cycle action](fdip-002P) leaves
constant fields unpenalized, so the full-space integral diverges.
Restricting to [mean-zero fields](fdip-0031) removes this direction,
but requires the subspace's own volume. The
[zero-mass cycle calculation](fdip-0038) gives the resulting normalizer
and a finite variance for the difference of opposite field values.}

\p{The [positive Gaussian law](fdip-0017) on the orthogonal complement
of the kernel yields this constrained probability and its
[pseudoinverse covariance](fdip-0032). [Kernel factorization](fdip-0033)
and [projected limits](fdip-0034) distinguish the divergent full
normalizer from finite difference observables. [Pinning a vertex](fdip-0035)
gives another constraint, with a generally different coordinate
covariance; the [two-vertex comparison](fdip-0036) makes the distinction explicit.
These choices also matter when eliminating
[singular directions](fdip-0039).}

